@jlqibm Thanks for inviting a review on #60914. I reviewed ff8499aa, including both dispatch branches and the new regression. The guards look correct from source inspection; I haven’t run GPU tests.

One non-blocking coverage question: the committed E=20/40 cases are both divisible by four, so they don’t exercise the newly selected shared-memory scalar-copy path. Have you also run a non-multiple-of-four case, such as E=21, with a shape confirmed to select blockRepeat > 1, for both quantizers?

At E=21, the old vector copy reaches indices 22..23 beyond the valid 0..21 range. A memcheck run with separately allocated E+1 offsets (rather than a view into a padded buffer) would complement the existing poisoned-tail test: output equality alone need not expose the extra shared-memory copies. If already covered by your standalone runs, documenting that case would be enough for this suggestion.
